# Security headers for static hosts that read this file (Netlify, Cloudflare
# Pages). GitHub Pages does not support custom response headers at all — if
# you're hosting there, these can't be applied; a small reverse proxy (e.g.
# Cloudflare in front of Pages) is the usual workaround.
#
# Why this file exists: index.html's Content-Security-Policy is delivered via
# a <meta> tag, which the CSP spec does not allow to carry frame-ancestors,
# sandbox, or report-uri/report-to. Those directives only take effect from a
# real HTTP response header, which only a server (or edge host) can send —
# hence this separate file rather than adding them to the meta tag.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()
